<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading">Lentil curry</h2>



<p>Next, add some lentils and a tin of tomatoes. I used <a href=3D"https://=
www.easycheesyvegetarian.com/different-types-of-lentils/">brown lentils</a>=
, which worked really nicely, but they do take half an hour or so to cook f=
ully (don=E2=80=99t worry, it=E2=80=99s almost entirely hands off!).</p>



<p>If you want this <a href=3D"https://www.easycheesyvegetarian.com/tarka-d=
al/">lentil curry</a> to be even quicker to make, you could use red lentils=
 instead =E2=80=93 they cook more quickly than brown, although they do end =
up with a different texture (they cook down a lot softer and mushier), so i=
t depends what you want the end result to be like.</p><div id=3D"AdThrive_C=
ontent_4_desktop" class=3D"adthrive-ad adthrive-sticky-container adthrive-c=
