 shot of lentil and halloumi curry in a pan topped with cilantro" class=3D"=
wp-image-13592"></figure>



<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading">How should I serve this lentil and halloumi =
curry?</h2>



<p>I served my lentil and halloumi curry simply with brown rice. White rice=
 would obviously be great too, as would some naan bread for dipping.</p><di=
v id=3D"AdThrive_Content_6_desktop" class=3D"adthrive-ad adthrive-sticky-co=
ntainer adthrive-content adthrive-content-6"></div>



<p>A scattering of fresh coriander (cilantro) on top is a must for any curr=
y, in my opinion =E2=80=93 the vibrant flavour of the herbs is great for fr=
eshening up any rich dish, as well as making it look much more attractive o=
n the plate (why is it that all the tastiest dishes just look like big bowl=
s of brown?!).</p>



<p>I also added a dollop of Greek yogurt on top of my halloumi curry =E2=80=
=93 I can=E2=80=99t resist an extra bit of creaminess. Feel free to use <a =
rel=3D"noreferrer noopener" aria-label=3D"raita (opens in a new tab)" href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raita" target=3D"_blank">raita</a> instea=
d, or anything similar!</p>



<p>And if you=E2=80=99re feeling <em>really</em> indulgent, a couple of oni=
on bhajis or <a href=3D"https://www.easycheesyvegetarian.com/tofu-spinach-s=
amosas/">vegetable samosas</a> on the side would be incredible.</p>



