<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading">How can I adapt this lentil and halloumi cur=
ry?</h2>



<p>This halloumi curry was such a triumph that I=E2=80=99m already thinking=
 of how I could alter it a little =E2=80=93 not because it needs altering, =
just because I=E2=80=99ll take any excuse to make it again!</p>



<p>Here are a few ideas:</p>



<ul class=3D"wp-block-list">
<li>Change the vegetables depending on what you have in your fridge =E2=80=
=93 almost anything will work well in a curry. Peppers, aubergine (eggplant=
), carrots, cauliflower, peas=E2=80=A6 it=E2=80=99s all welcome.</li>



<li>Switch the spices for a combination that feels more <a href=3D"https://=
www.easycheesyvegetarian.com/category/cuisine/texmex-recipes/">Tex-Mex</a>,=
 and serve your spicy halloumi with some sour cream and tortilla chips for =
dipping.</li>



<li>If you can=E2=80=99t find halloumi, use <a href=3D"https://www.easychee=
syvegetarian.com/30-minute-saag-paneer/">paneer</a> instead =E2=80=93 it=E2=
=80=99s not got as much flavour, but will work just as well in the tasty sa=
uce.</li>



<li>Make sure your lentil and halloumi curry is extra thick, and serve it w=
rapped in <a href=3D"https://www.easycheesyvegetarian.com/indian-roasted-ch=
ickpea-flatbreads/">Indian-style flatbreads</a> (e.g. chapatis) with a doll=
op of yogurt and some salad.</li>
</ul><div id=3D"AdThrive_Content_8_desktop" class=3D"adthrive-ad adthrive-s=
ticky-container adthrive-content adthrive-content-8"></div>



<p>Let me know if you have any other bright ideas!</p>



